      },
      "message": "fix(pocket): kernel pocket levels enter over the floor above; fig8 plans\n\nThe fig8 pocket on the kernel showed three defects of the first recipe:\n- the stock less the band left a sliver loop, which the selection\n  refused: the K1 adapter now drops loops thinner than 0.1 um;\n- the verifier read each air entry outside the stock as a gouge of the\n  stock edge: the arm now gives it the pocket area and the air round\n  the stock (kernel_pocket_reach), the part walls stay judged;\n- each lower level entered from over the stock top, so its helix ran\n  through the levels already cut and crossed their cuts: a lower level\n  now enters over the floor of the level above where its approach\n  stands on a cut of every level above (else from over the stock top).\n  The converter takes the proved top of each level (LevelPlan::top_z)\n  and still refuses an approach under it.\n\nThe fig8 pin records a refusal by name of a kernel stage (the Inside\nstart, #4324) and names the entry lead crossings of #4300.\n\nRefs #3752\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
